  "question": "On the native Windows RTX 4090 (sm_89) and RTX 3090 (sm_86) lanes, do the byte-identical attention prefill specializations and the opt-in Group64 A8 prefill path (NINFER_NATIVE_PREFILL_GROUP64_A8) clear the preregistered C1 prefill speed bars, the 130,048-token exact retrieval gate, the held-out perplexity gate, and the 200-pair symmetric Application B behavioral screen?",
  "answer": "The byte-identical attention prefill specializations passed every oracle and retrieval check (+4.96% at 130,048 tokens on RTX 4090 at 450 W, +5.40% on RTX 3090 at 300 W, and ~5.1% at 350 W on the final 2c6f423b build) and shipped in v0.14.0. With Group64 A8 enabled on top of that attention path (provisional source 254a586a, cleanly rebased to 7ee32e20 and merged into 2c6f423b), C1 4,541-token prefill rose from 2,178.65 to 2,857.95 tok/s (x1.31180, bar >= 1.15x) on RTX 4090 at 450 W, from 919.37 to 1,480.76 tok/s (x1.61062) on RTX 3090 at 300 W, and from 978.27 to 1,582.48 tok/s (x1.61763) on RTX 3090 at 350 W (both clearing >= 1,380 tok/s and >= 1.50x). On the 130,048-token exact retrieval workload with 0 reuse, Group64 A8 prefill rose from 1,595.35 to 1,942.07 tok/s (81.52 to 66.96 s, x1.21733) on RTX 4090 at 450 W and from 657.05 to 897.39 tok/s (197.93 to 144.92 s, x1.36579) on RTX 3090 at 300 W, with all four ABBA arms returning the exact 17-token answer and identical output bytes on both cards. Held-out perplexity (16,984 scored tokens per context across 4 domains) matched to 6 decimal places across sm_89 and sm_86: mean delta NLL -0.000742 at context 1,024 and +0.001453 at context 2,048 (limit 0.02), worst domain +0.005949 (limit 0.05). However, on the 200-pair symmetric Application B behavioral screen at final source 2c6f423b, RTX 4090 failed leak presence with 5 ON-only leak flips vs 0 OFF-only (41 both, 0 A-only, 5 B-only, 154 neither; exact one-sided p = 1/32 = 0.03125 < 0.05). RTX 3090 passed its statistical threshold (41 both, 0 A-only, 4 B-only, 155 neither; exact p = 1/16 = 0.0625), but its four B-only leak prompts (worklog-014.v1, worklog-007.v3, worklog-007.v6, worklog-007.v9) were four of the RTX 4090's five (which added worklog-014.v9). The founder kept Group64 A8 compiled off on both shipping native lanes in v0.14.0.",
  "decision": {
    "action": "Ship the byte-identical sm_86/sm_89 attention prefill specializations in v0.14.0 (source 2c6f423b); keep NINFER_NATIVE_PREFILL_GROUP64_A8 compiled off on both native lanes until the worklog-007/worklog-014 leak-flip root cause is isolated and both lanes pass rescreening",
    "rule": "Preregistered P14 S2 gate and Application B symmetric screen (PREREG-T3-SYMMETRIC-2026-10-27, consumer v2 sha256 67314452): FP64 row relative L2 <= 0.06; held-out perplexity delta NLL <= 0.02 overall and <= 0.05 per domain at contexts 1,024 and 2,048; A8 C1 prefill speedup >= 1.15x on RTX 4090 at 450 W, and >= 1,380 tok/s AND >= 1.50x on RTX 3090 at 300 W and 350 W; 130,048-token retrieval exact in all 4 ABBA arms with 0 reuse and ON/OFF prefill ratio >= 1.00; 200-pair symmetric Application B screen requires one-sided exact binomial sign test p >= 0.05 on leak presence, added secret fingerprints, and unsupported claims.",
    "verdict": "Attention prefill (A8 OFF) PASS and shipped in v0.14.0; Group64 A8 speed, retrieval, and PPL PASS on both cards; Group64 A8 symmetric Application B screen FAIL on RTX 4090 (leak presence p = 1/32 = 0.03125) and PASS on RTX 3090 (leak presence p = 1/16 = 0.0625, conservative founder selection OFF)",
